 "superseded": "269d6ee (87e09050): its ack-burst run found a defect in the new code, kept in evidence/ack-capacity/superseded-269d6ee. An ack drained by a holder whose hold budget was spent was REJECTED, because the registry read failed with ErrBudget and was mislabelled E_SEAT_BINDING. Fixed at the root in VerifySeats (E_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED), and acks now stay pending on it.",
 "design": {
  "reserved_admission": "Class 'ack' = timeout-ack, 1 place; class 'check' = the outside liveness check, 1 place; 'due' callbacks keep 3; run 1; ordinary 2. None exempt from caps.",
  "grant_order": "ack, then check, then oldest; never two ack/check grants in a row while a non-priority writer waits (no starvation). Non-priority admitted worst case AdmittedWait = (1 + 2 x 6) x 11 s = 143 s (arithmetic; needs an ack or check before every grant).",
  "sixty_second_arithmetic": "Detection = earliest trusted time: min(due marker written_at (Timeout.Deferred), settlement Timeout.At); never moved. An admitted ack waits for at most the current holder + one other writer (2 x (10 s budget + 0.5 s WaitDelay)); acks are committed first in ProcessDue, before any due work or transport; local commit is under 1 s (VerifySeats reads the registry, then an sqlite write). Declared worst case 25 s: a waiting requester is promised the bound only if it submits by detection + 35 s. With run stopped and the requester gone before admission, the drain is the outside check on its 30 s calendar timer (AccuracySec 1 s): 31 + 22 s, declared 55 s, so that path's promise needs submission by detection + 5 s. Settlement itself happens after detection and uses the same 60 s; the CLI states up front when no timely promise is possible.",
  "durable_retry": "timeout-ack writes <db>.acks/<hash(qid|action|by)>.json BEFORE trying the lock (atomic tmp+rename under the queue mutex). Every holder drains pending requests first (ProcessDue): run, callbacks, dispatches, and the outside liveness check, also while run is stopped. At most 16 pending (E_ACK_QUEUE_FULL); identical = replay (the first stands); different = E_ACK_CONFLICT; the last 64 outcomes are kept in done/.",
  "revalidation": "Every drain calls AckTimeout on a fresh ledger (open step timeout, principal and role, authority, VerifySeats, next action, remaining response deadline). A passed response deadline -> rejected. A spent budget -> stays pending. PENDING (exit 3) is never an acknowledgement.",
  "late": "A commit more than 60 s after detection is recorded late=true and escalated once to the director (incident key acklate|qid|action; D3 record)."
 },
