  "unit": "go test 0 FAIL (go-test.txt). New tests: internal/loop/ack_p12_test.go (grant order and no-starvation, classes, earliest detection, pending not an ack until committed by another holder, replay/conflict/queue bound, forged/expired/late with escalation, a spent budget stays pending).",
  "mutation": "final run on f7d2c72: 147 of 147 Go mutants caught; earlier run on dbcf5df: 143/147, where the 4 misses were NOT runs: 3 did not build and 1 anchor had moved, all re-anchored. 11 new mutants.",
  "conformance": "125/125, 1751 steps, rc 0, exact binary 77c46332",
  "parity": "host-parity.txt",
  "regressions_on_77c46332": "regress/: CLI timeout idle and refused, with the ack rules through the new request path (wrong actor rejected, conflict rejected); busy-callback race; writer race; stopped-mode no-ack escalation (duty +60 s, director +120 s, no incident); SIGTERM stop. Cleanup by exact path (cleanup.txt).",
  "real_process": {
   "harness": "ackharness.sh + ack-driver.sh + run-all.sh + analyse.py + ack-analyse.py, pre-registered in commits 07087471, bc49b470, 59e643e0 before each run",
   "ack-burst": "14 accepted due markers, 40 s outside stall, slow ordinary dispatches, outside check every 30 s in its own process: every committed ack <= 10 s after submission. Timely: submitted det+30, committed det+34 (settlement took 30 s). Near the boundary: det+34 -> det+34. Late: det+62 -> det+63, late and escalated once. Requester SIGKILLed after PENDING -> committed by another holder. Duplicate -> 1 ack. Conflict -> E_ACK_CONFLICT. Forged -> rejected. Expired -> rejected. Run stopped plus requester killed -> the outside check committed it 10 s later. Run restarted. The check's admission-to-lock max was 19.9 s with the callback places full. All 14 markers settled; 0 duplicate notice effects.",
   "ack-quiet": "no stall: timely det+5 -> det+6; boundary det+34 -> det+34; late det+62 -> late and escalated; stopped-run drain 6 s after submission; max commit-after-submit 1 s.",
   "timestamps": "detection (ledger), submission and commit (request and done/ records), admission and acquire (lock.log per pid): */ack-table.txt, */acks.log, */lock.log"
  }
 },
 "residuals": [
  "The non-priority worst case is now 143 s (arithmetic). It exceeds the liveness StaleAfter of 100 s only if an ack or check arrives before every grant. The heartbeat stays truthful (it would alarm). Measured run waits: max 44 s.",
  "If NO process can take the ledger lock at all (for example an outside holder that never releases), a pending request is not committed and not escalated by the loop. The liveness check's own failure is then the alarm. Host assumption: the outside check's calendar timer runs.",
  "A timely human response is not claimed: the promise covers only the scheduling after submission, and it depends on settlement latency (measured up to 40 s with the 40 s stall).",
